{"seconds": 70.4, "exit": 0, "final": "So after 3...Bxe2, White can recapture with 4.Nxe2, and material is roughly: Black up the rook minus the bishop, so up a rook for nothing essentially.\n\nThis confirms **Qxd3+** is the winning move. The tactic is that the d3 pawn is pinned and undefended, so it can be captured with check, and the follow-up with the bishop creates devastating threats.\n\n**Coaching note (under 80 words):**\n\"The d3 pawn is pinned to White's king by your bishop on h7\u2014it can't really be defended. When the pawn is pinned along a line, attack it immediately! Here, Qxd3+ forces White's rook to recapture, then Bxd3+ wins it with check. The bishop's presence on h7 creates a tactical weakness on d3. Always scan for loose pieces on pinning lines\u2014they're targets.\"\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"Qxd3+\", \"line\": [\"Qxd3+\", \"Rxd3\", \"Bxd3+\", \"Ka1\", \"Bxe2\"], \"motifs\": [\"pin\", \"hangingPiece\"]}\n```", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "2kr4/3nn1Bb/2p1pp1p/1p1pP3/5P1H/bPqP1N2/P3Q1B1/1K1R2NR b - - 4 23"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "2kr4/3nn1Bb/2p1pp1p/1p1pP3/5P1H/bPqP1N2/P3Q1B1/1K1R2NR b - - 4 23"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-legal_moves", "args": {"fen": "2kr4/3nn1Bb/2p1pp1p/1p1pP3/5P1H/bPqP1N2/P3Q1B1/1K1R2NR b - - 4 23"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "2kr4/3nn1Bb/2p1pp1p/1p1pP3/5P2/bPqP1N2/P3Q1B1/1K1R2NR b - - 4 23"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "2kr4/3nn1Bb/2p1pp1p/1p1pP3/5P2/bPqP1N2/P3Q1B1/1K1R2NR b - - 4 23"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-legal_moves", "args": {"fen": "2kr4/3nn1Bb/2p1pp1p/1p1pP3/5P2/bPqP1N2/P3Q1B1/1K1R2NR b - - 4 23"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "2kr4/3nn1Bb/2p1pp1p/1p1pP3/5P2/bPqP1N2/P3Q1B1/1K1R2NR b - - 4 23", "square": "c3"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "2kr4/3nn1Bb/2p1pp1p/1p1pP3/5P2/bPqP1N2/P3Q1B1/1K1R2NR b - - 4 23", "square": "a3"}}, {"tool": "